---
// Recording consent, from the README's Meetings ("Recording is your decision"). The offer is drawn
// in HTML with the app's own words (the Drop's consent offer, Mac, as rendered by the app).
---

<section class="section" id="consent" aria-labelledby="consent-title">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="consent-title">Recording a call is your&nbsp;decision.</h2>
        <p>
          When an app has held the microphone for three seconds, Inkwell follows that app’s choice, set from the
          Drop or in Settings > Meetings.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="choices">
        <b>Ask</b> is the default: the Drop offers to record. <b>Always</b> records, and the first time it does, the
        Drop reminds you to tell the others. <b>Never</b> leaves that app’s calls alone. For the first minute of a
        meeting, <b>Stop and delete</b> ends it and deletes it as if it had never been made.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="offer wide-only" role="img" aria-label="The Drop’s offer: Zoom opened the microphone. Recording keeps both sides on this Mac. Tell the others you are recording. Buttons: Record this call, Not this one, Always for Zoom, Never for Zoom.">
      <span class="src">Zoom opened the microphone</span>
      <span class="say">Recording keeps both sides on this Mac. Tell the others you are recording.</span>
      <span class="acts"><span>Record this call</span><span>Not this one</span><span>Always for Zoom</span><span>Never for Zoom</span></span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
